2. Nf3 { The White knight travels from g1 to f3. The letter N means knight; f3 is its destination. } 2... Nc6 { Black develops the b8 knight to c6. Black uses exactly the same square names as White. } *

[Event "Chess, Clearly: lesson 2"]
[Site "https://knightway8.github.io/chess15/lessons/02-a-rook-stops-at-the-first-obstacle.html"]
